  [ok] GPU: AMD Radeon 8060S (Ryzen AI Max, Strix Halo, gfx1151), unified memory: 1.0 GB BIOS carve-out + 118 GB shared with the RAM, 119 GB usable by the GPU, gfx1151 (AMD: docs/STRIX_HALO.md)
  Strix Halo (gfx1151, Ryzen AI Max): the CPU and the GPU share one memory pool (124 GB seen by the OS + a 1.0 GB BIOS carve-out), so the model's experts live in that pool and the expert cache is sized from the memory the OS can give back, not from the carve-out.
  The engine is compiled here for gfx1151 (experimental, measured on one machine): see docs/STRIX_HALO.md.
  Recommended model: UD-IQ4_XS (the one docs/STRIX_HALO.md measures); the menus list the others.
  [ok] RAM: 124 GB
  [ok] CPU: AMD RYZEN AI MAX+ 395 w/ Radeon 8060S (AVX-512)

=== Step 2: your choices ===
  [ok] model: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (Unsloth)

  1) UD-IQ4_XS (recommended) ~4-bit i-quant (Unsloth Dynamic), between IQ3_S and UD-Q4_K_XL in quality; on a PC with less than ~80 GB of RAM part of its experts are read from the SSD; download 94 GB, keeps ~55 GB of its 60 GB of experts in RAM
  2) UD-Q4_K_XL (recommended) 4-bit (Unsloth Dynamic): K-quant experts, between UD-IQ4_XS and UD-Q5_K_XL in quality; download 111 GB, keeps ~71 GB of its 77 GB of experts in RAM
  3) UD-Q5_K_XL 5-bit (Unsloth Dynamic): Q5_K experts with Q8_0 downs, close to Q8_0 in quality; download 158 GB, keeps ~91 GB of its 98 GB of experts in RAM
  4) UD-Q6_K_XL 6-bit (Unsloth Dynamic): Q6_K experts with Q8_0 downs; download 169 GB, keeps ~100 GB of its 109 GB of experts in RAM
  5) Q8_0 8-bit, the reference quality (every expert Q8_0); for a 192 GB PC; download 188 GB, keeps ~100 GB of its 128 GB of experts in RAM   <- needs 136 GB RAM, you have 124
  [ok] RAM budget: 71 GiB of UD-Q4_K_XL's experts in RAM, the rest read from the model files on the SSD
